.TH SECTORREC 1 "October 2026" "SectorRec 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sectorrec \- guided file recovery and disk imaging interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sectorrec
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SectorRec provides a graphical interface for recovering deleted files
using The Sleuth Kit or PhotoRec, locating lost partitions via TestDisk,
and creating disk images with GNU ddrescue.
Both Debian package editions invoke system-installed recovery tools.
Debian editions use Polkit for fixed-purpose privileged helpers.
On desktop, Polkit asks for administrator approval once per app session on the first privileged
operation; subsequent operations reuse that session until the application closes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Display demo data without accessing physical media.
.TP
.B --list-devices
List recognized devices in JSON format.
.TP
.B --ui desktop
Use the desktop interface. The Cardputer package defaults to framebuffer.
.TP
.B --help
Show the available command line options.
.SH SECURITY
Never save recovered files to the source disk. Physical disk authorization
may require a single Polkit authentication per application session.
The restricted root broker exits when SectorRec closes; no permanent
user permissions are created.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fls (1),
.BR icat (1),
.BR testdisk (8),
.BR photorec (8),
.BR ddrescue (1)
.SH AUTHOR
SectorRec contributors
